{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/498879-vampire-and-werewolf-transformation-diagram-for-crossover-games-large-image","id":498879,"title":"Vampire and Werewolf transformation diagram for crossover games (large image)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-01T08:13:39-07:00","id":498879,"title":"Vampire and Werewolf transformation diagram for crossover games (large image)","content":"Hi !<br /> <br /> I was afraid my new players wouldn't understand the complex interactions between vampires and werewolves, and their many minor templates, so I put together this diagram showing all possible interactions between the two creature types. Hopefully, I didn't miss anything important. Enjoy!<br /> <br /> <b>Fairly Large Edit:</b> Here's the expanded diagram:<br /> <br /> First &quot;expanded&quot; version: <a href=\"http://i58.tinypic.com/2gv37n6.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://i58.tinypic.com/2gv37n6.jpg</a><br /> Second &quot;expanded&quot; version: <a href=\"http://i61.tinypic.com/2r7txqb.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://i61.tinypic.com/2r7txqb.jpg</a><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i61.tinypic.com/2r7txqb.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> For those interested in the original versions (Vampires and Werewolves only):<br /> <br /> First version: <a href=\"http://i61.tinypic.com/2vci33p.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://i61.tinypic.com/2vci33p.jpg</a><br /> Second version: <a href=\"http://i62.tinypic.com/20uu6br.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://i62.tinypic.com/20uu6br.jpg</a><br /> Third version: <a href=\"http://i60.tinypic.com/25p7cbl.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://i60.tinypic.com/25p7cbl.jpg</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5602,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","user":"BarbeChenue","date":".  Expanded the Diagram 05-07-2015, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T09:30:46-07:00","id":498993,"title":"","content":"I like this.<br /> <br /> Would you kill me if I asked you to add Mages and Proximi to the chart when Mage 2e comes out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T10:21:52-07:00","id":499083,"title":"","content":"I also have a problem with &quot;cursed&quot; state sort of part... Most of these could be considered &quot;cursed&quot; (except for Any Human)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T10:27:57-07:00","id":499092,"title":"","content":"I thought that was a little odd too. Also the implication that a Wolf-Blooded who fails their First Change becomes something other than a Wolf-Blooded. I wonder if there is another way to visually communicate that after a failed First Change you can't become a werewolf, without making it a separate category from Wolf-Blooded. Other than those minor nitpicks, I love this!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T10:37:34-07:00","id":499104,"title":"","content":"I'll re-work this in order to integrate the changes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would you kill me if I asked you to add Mages and Proximi to the chart when Mage 2e comes out? </div> </div> </div>I think I'll need some more info on those, as I am totally unfamiliar with Mages and especially Proximi. What is the trigger of the transformation? Can you be further transformed into something else? What are the &quot;stacking&quot; rules in place (can you be both wolf-blooded and Proximi, for ex.) ? Can you become a Vampire if you are a Mage? Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T10:41:37-07:00","id":499111,"title":"","content":"That's why I'm asking for it when Mage 2e comes out; we don't exactly <i>know</i> at the moment. Well, other than the fact that anyone who isn't a Major Template can go through a Mystery Play and become a Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T11:10:00-07:00","id":499130,"title":"","content":"In the meantime, here's the edited version. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I guess the major templates act as a point of no return, so if you're transformed into a major one, there is no going back, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T11:16:06-07:00","id":499136,"title":"","content":"Correct.<br /> <br /> Though you could theoretically die and be resurrected through one of the more powerful Numina, Resurrection. When this happens your template is removed and you are alive again a semi-ordinary human.<br /> <br /> p230, 'This Numen \u2014 only available to Rank 4+ angels and spirits of healing \u2014 raises the dead. The Numen costs 10 Essence to use and the activation roll is penalized by one die per day that the subject has been dead. Supernatural beings that have already died as part of their transformation \u2014 vampires, mummies and Sin-Eaters \u2014 can\u2019t be resurrected, nor can anyone who died of natural causes. Other supernatural beings lose their powers when resurrected. Mages become Sleepwalkers and werewolves, wolf-blooded.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-01-2015, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T11:17:53-07:00","id":499137,"title":"","content":"Well...<br /> <br /> There actually <i>is</i> for Werewolves. If they die and a high-rank Spirit of Life/Healing/Whatevs uses the Resurrection Numen on them, they come back as Wolfblooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T12:03:38-07:00","id":499210,"title":"","content":"This is awesome, though I realise I should go back and re-ead about the minor templates.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/498879-vampire-and-werewolf-transformation-diagram-for-crossover-games-large-image?p=499130#post499130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the meantime, here's the edited version. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I guess the major templates act as a point of no return, so if you're transformed into a major one, there is no going back, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Promethean that become mortal can become any of the major templates, likewise, if a sin-eater's geist leaves (I think) .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5544-ancientswordrage","name":"AncientSwordRage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T12:45:09-07:00","id":499262,"title":"","content":"It's a cool graphic. I look forward to seeing a fully fleshed out one some day with all the lines involved.<br /> <br /> I'm a little confused as to why the Wolf-Blooded fluff names are included. In re-reading that section of the book, it just seemed like &quot;Sons of the Moon&quot; and &quot;Daughters of the Wolf&quot; were just Wolf-Blooded that had werewolves or other Wolf-Blooded in their family tree roughly categorized by Tell. &quot;Orphans&quot; was just used to say that some Wolf-Blooded were born that way even though there was no wolf in their blood-line. &quot;Adoption&quot; was another way of saying &quot;spontaneous Wolf-Blooded&quot; which are described elsewhere in the book (mostly from dramatic Lunacy failures, though the fluff there indicates that maybe there are other in-roads).<br /> <br /> Are you planning to actually use those words in play ever? <br /> Either way, I think &quot;Orphans&quot; should probably come in with the Sons and Daughters along with a note of &quot;Born this way&quot; and the &quot;Adopted&quot; should get a note of &quot;Spontaneous Wolf-Blood Development&quot; with or without a note that Lunacy or Luna or something else could cause it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T12:55:22-07:00","id":499269,"title":"","content":"So basically you can be a <b>Promethean </b>redeemed into a <b>Human </b>who is an [adoptive <b>Wolf-Blooded</b>, who became a <b>Ghoul </b>temporarily [n times], who turned into a <b>Werewolf</b>, who died and was Resurrected into a <b>Wolf-Blooded</b>] [n times] who <u>at some point</u> failed his/her [second] First Change, became a <b>Ghoul </b>once again [n times], died as a Ghoul, became a <b>Revenant</b>, then diablerized some poor vampire and became one of the <b>Kindred</b>. <i>Only then </i>have you reached the point of no return.<br /> <br /> O_O","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T13:00:20-07:00","id":499277,"title":"","content":"That seems like a highly unlikely scenario, but yes.<br /> Well, maybe. I actually have no idea how Ghouls work.<br /> Also, do Vampires die? Is there any reason why a dead Vampire can't be made into a Promethean again?<br /> Either way, you're missing the beginning part of the Promethean redeemed into the Human getting killed and made into a Promethean again. That happened in the 1E fiction at the beginning and end of the book. It was really good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4563,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","user":"TerraBen","date":". 05-01-2015, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T13:12:32-07:00","id":499291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/498879-vampire-and-werewolf-transformation-diagram-for-crossover-games-large-image?p=499277#post499277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, do Vampires die? Is there any reason why a dead Vampire can't be made into a Promethean again?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no reason the parts couldn't be made into a Promethean, but it wouldn't really be the same person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T14:12:43-07:00","id":499377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/498879-vampire-and-werewolf-transformation-diagram-for-crossover-games-large-image?p=499262#post499262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a cool graphic. I look forward to seeing a fully fleshed out one some day with all the lines involved.<br /> <br /> I'm a little confused as to why the Wolf-Blooded fluff names are included. In re-reading that section of the book, it just seemed like &quot;Sons of the Moon&quot; and &quot;Daughters of the Wolf&quot; were just Wolf-Blooded that had werewolves or other Wolf-Blooded in their family tree roughly categorized by Tell. &quot;Orphans&quot; was just used to say that some Wolf-Blooded were born that way even though there was no wolf in their blood-line. &quot;Adoption&quot; was another way of saying &quot;spontaneous Wolf-Blooded&quot; which are described elsewhere in the book (mostly from dramatic Lunacy failures, though the fluff there indicates that maybe there are other in-roads).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, these aren't templates in themselves. Putting them in seems needlessly confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T15:29:13-07:00","id":499444,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised that there is no line between 'human' and the 'First Change' stages. Humans do not have to become Wolf-Blooded before experiencing the First Change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T15:32:14-07:00","id":499449,"title":"","content":"Well, I thought of the diagram as an aid for my players, and I thought they'd like to hear about the multiple possible origins of the Wolf-Blooded, including the non-human mythological ones. The diagram is meant to avoid being too immersion-breaking while clearing things up a bit.<br /> <br /> I could perhaps make another version later, once other supernatural templates are added. I admit I'll need the room ! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T15:47:07-07:00","id":499456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/498879-vampire-and-werewolf-transformation-diagram-for-crossover-games-large-image?p=499291#post499291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no reason the parts couldn't be made into a Promethean, but it wouldn't really be the same person.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point. They do sometimes end up with residual memories, though. If I'm not mistaken, part of the Pilgrimage can sometimes be figuring out who they were and how that effects who they are now.<br /> <br /> Other than that, though, I don't of a way to stop being a vampire. Let's see how far we can take this, though:<br /> <br /> Promethan - Redeemed -<br /> Human - Lunacy/Adoption -<br /> Wolf-Blooded - First Change -<br /> Werewolf - Death/Ressurection - <br /> Wolf-Blooded - Awakening - <br /> Mage - Death/Ressurection - <br /> Sleep-Walker - Death/Bargain - <br /> Sin-Eater - Un-Binding - <br /> Human - Fed Vitae - <br /> Ghoul - Death - <br /> Revenant - Diablerie - <br /> Vampire<br /> <br /> Is there a minor template for Changelings to fall back to if they get Ressurected? They're not called out as imune to that Numina. I don't see how we could fit Mummy or Demon into the mix, though, given their relatively unique origins and life cycles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T15:55:47-07:00","id":499461,"title":"","content":"Demon has a similar problem to dying and being made into a Promethean. The character could sell their soul to a Demon and become one of its Covers, but then it's no longer really <i>them</i>, it just a Demon that sometimes looks like them and has their memories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T16:24:01-07:00","id":499478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/498879-vampire-and-werewolf-transformation-diagram-for-crossover-games-large-image?p=499449#post499449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could perhaps make another version later, once other supernatural templates are added. I admit I'll need the room ! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Your thread title does promise a large image. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T20:29:54-07:00","id":499711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/498879-vampire-and-werewolf-transformation-diagram-for-crossover-games-large-image?p=499277#post499277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, do Vampires die? Is there any reason why a dead Vampire can't be made into a Promethean again?</div> </div> </div> </div>It can, and in fact, they have stats for a hypothetical &quot;Vampiric Promethean&quot; in Saturnine Night (p. 35).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T23:53:47-07:00","id":499922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/498879-vampire-and-werewolf-transformation-diagram-for-crossover-games-large-image?p=499461#post499461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon has a similar problem to dying and being made into a Promethean. The character could sell their soul to a Demon and become one of its Covers, but then it's no longer really <i>them</i>, it just a Demon that sometimes looks like them and has their memories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the demon doesn't even have their memories, only what the demon was able to suss out through investigation before coming to claim its due.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T00:52:11-07:00","id":499974,"title":"","content":"I presume that a changeling resurrected by that numen would come back as a fae touched mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T02:08:31-07:00","id":500022,"title":"","content":"Okay, maybe a dumb question, but can a Ghoul undergo the First Change?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T04:55:27-07:00","id":500152,"title":"","content":"I don't think they can but I can't actually find a reference either way in the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T05:01:16-07:00","id":500161,"title":"","content":"As far as I understand it, anyone not already fitted with a major template can end up with one. So a Ghoul could Awaken, a Sleep-Walker could go through the First Change, and a Wolf-Blooded could be stolen by the gentry or bargained with by a geist if it would make the story more interesting. The minor-to-major template relationship is more a matter of proximity than of destiny. As mentioned earlier, Mummy and Demon are harder to get into than the others as they are either literally from ancient Egypt or were once clockwork ethereals. Those aside, anyone has the potential to end up as anything, theoretically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T07:35:45-07:00","id":500326,"title":"","content":"And we've not even mentioned the Sea of Fragments, in the underworld. The vampire could go there to become human again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5544-ancientswordrage","name":"AncientSwordRage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T08:17:09-07:00","id":500377,"title":"","content":"Or at the very least, an entirely mundane corpse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T08:46:22-07:00","id":500450,"title":"","content":"OK, how many minor and major templates should I expect to put on the same diagram? And I'm talking &quot;playable ones&quot; that are popular enough and have a modicum of interconnectedness.<br /> <br /> Lines:<br /> <br /> Vampire (<b>done</b>),<br /> Werewolf (<b>done</b>),<br /> Mage (<i>awaiting 2e</i>; minor: Proximus or Sleepwalker / major: Mage ),<br /> Changeling (? minor: Fey-Touched / major: Changeling ?),<br /> Promethean (? minor: ?? / major: Promethean ?),<br /> Demon (? minor: Stigmatic / major: Demon ?),<br /> Sin-Eaters (? minor: ?? / major: Sin-Eater ?),<br /> Hunters (??) (they have a few minor templates, like Slashers, I'd like to add),<br /> Mummy (? minor: ?? / major: Mummy ?)<br /> <br /> I'll probably end up putting all the templates that interact together in identical ways in the same boxes to save on space. All the non-supernatural (Ripper) / supernatural (Scourge) Slasher templates (Undertakings) would end up in the same two boxes, unless they interact with others in mechanically distinct ways.<br /> <br /> So yes... the stacking potential of minor templates is not to be trifled with... I mean, if a human Mask wolf-blooded, fey-touched, proximus, ghoul is possible... O_O","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5602,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","user":"BarbeChenue","date":". 05-02-2015, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T08:57:25-07:00","id":500462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/498879-vampire-and-werewolf-transformation-diagram-for-crossover-games-large-image?p=500450#post500450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, how many minor and major templates should I expect to put on the same diagram? And I'm talking &quot;playable ones&quot; that are popular enough and have a modicum of interconnectedness.<br /> <br /> Lines:<br /> <br /> Vampire (<b>done</b>),<br /> Werewolf (<b>done</b>),<br /> Mage (<i>awaiting 2e</i>; minor: Proximus or Sleepwalker / major: Mage ),<br /> Changeling (? minor: Fey-Touched / major: Changeling ?),<br /> Promethean (? minor: ?? / major: Promethean ?),<br /> Demon (? minor: Stigmatic / major: Demon ?),<br /> Sin-Eaters (? minor: ?? / major: Sin-Eater ?),<br /> Hunters (??) (they have a few minor templates, like Slashers, I'd like to add),<br /> Mummy (? minor: ?? / major: Mummy ?)<br /> <br /> I'll probably end up putting all the templates that interact together in identical ways in the same boxes to save on space. All the non-supernatural (Ripper) / supernatural (Scourge) Slasher templates (Undertakings) would end up in the same two boxes, unless they interact with others in mechanically distinct ways.<br /> <br /> So yes... the stacking potential of minor templates is not to be trifled with... I mean, if a human Mask wolf-blooded, fey-touched, proximus, ghoul is possible... O_O</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The minor splat for Promethean appears to be mortal alchemists, and I think you could arguably consider Abmortals and those possessed by ghosts as minor splats for Geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T09:07:48-07:00","id":500466,"title":"","content":"It'll be interesting to see if the changeling 2e book has anything of fae touched. As is the 1st edition stuff is... lacking. <br /> <br /> 'Course one could argue that by certain standards Changeling itself is the minor counterpart to True Fae, but that's not so much minor/major as major/ohgodwhatthefuck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T09:31:54-07:00","id":500491,"title":"","content":"Well there's a full 10k word appendix blocked out for them in the outline, so I think it's a safe bet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T12:34:59-07:00","id":500609,"title":"","content":"There's not explicitly a minor template for Geist yet, but everyone who becomes a Sin-Eater has to have a supernatural Merit or two before their Bargain. It's not something typically played out or talked about much, but it is part of their splat that they had some supernatural/psychic sensitivity while they were still &quot;normal&quot;. If you're adding them to the diagram, it'd be worth noting that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T13:52:14-07:00","id":500749,"title":"","content":"Oh, and <a href=\"https://&quot;http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/62318/World-of-Darkness-Immortals\" target=\"_blank\">Immortals</a>...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5544-ancientswordrage","name":"AncientSwordRage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T00:13:12-07:00","id":501454,"title":"","content":"Yeah i guess one would have to play it by ear for sin-eaters, but I'd guess in all likelihood that most of them had either unseen sense-ghost, medium, or both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T13:33:38-07:00","id":502091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/498879-vampire-and-werewolf-transformation-diagram-for-crossover-games-large-image?p=499444#post499444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprised that there is no line between 'human' and the 'First Change' stages. Humans do not have to become Wolf-Blooded before experiencing the First Change.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't aware of that fact. Is that from a 1e book? Cause I didn't see anything in the 2e core that suggested this was the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T13:36:32-07:00","id":502093,"title":"","content":"Luna does what Luna wants. Luna don't give a fuck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T13:43:46-07:00","id":502126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/498879-vampire-and-werewolf-transformation-diagram-for-crossover-games-large-image?p=502093#post502093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luna does what Luna wants. Luna don't give a fuck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but as far as I know that falls under ST fiat and doesn't really need to be accounted for in the diagram. Some people become vampires without being embraced eithervtraditionally or posthumously, but I don't think that needs to be on the chart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T13:53:37-07:00","id":502138,"title":"","content":"Well, one's a rare, near-legendary event. The other happens fairly regularly.<br /> <br /> Actually should people embraced using Synthesis have a separate line? I'm not sure if &quot;Strix corpse-puppet&quot; counts as a template or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T13:55:23-07:00","id":502142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/498879-vampire-and-werewolf-transformation-diagram-for-crossover-games-large-image?p=502091#post502091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't aware of that fact. Is that from a 1e book?</div> </div> </div> </div>From the 1e core onward wordings are used that talk about wolf-blooded and pre-Change werewolves as though they were similar but distinct categories of being and nothing in 2e contradicts this. Further\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WtF1e Core, p44, &quot;Childhood&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although werewolves can generally recognize the scent of a fellow werewolf, this ability is much more difficult before the Change. It becomes possible only within a lunar month or so of when the First Change is coming. <b>A werewolf parent has no reliable way of knowing if a newborn, or even a young child, is truly Uratha or not; the child might smell like one of the wolf-blooded, but even that\u2019s not a reliable sign. Many werewolves don\u2019t display any sign of the wolf blood until the Change approaches. </b>Likewise, the spirits don\u2019t tend to recognize a nascent werewolf up until about the last moon before the First Change \u2014 and the Change doesn\u2019t happen at a predictable point in life.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WtF1e Core p79-80, &quot;Merits: Wolf-Blooded&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This Merit can also apply to a werewolf character who has yet to undergo the First Change.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's like the supernatural traits that frequently mark a Bound-to-be: oftentimes it only shows up shortly before the main Event.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T14:10:26-07:00","id":502157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/498879-vampire-and-werewolf-transformation-diagram-for-crossover-games-large-image?p=502142#post502142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the 1e core onward wordings are used that talk about wolf-blooded and pre-Change werewolves as though they were similar but distinct categories of being and nothing in 2e contradicts this. Further\u2026<br /> <br /> It's like the supernatural traits that frequently mark a Bound-to-be: oftentimes it only shows up shortly before the main Event.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, ok. Thanks for pointing those out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T03:38:48-07:00","id":502715,"title":"","content":"In a way enscorcereled mortals could be considered 'fey-touched'. They are basically any mortal that through a deal with a Fae or Changeling can now fully see the world of the Fae. Mind you, that particular template can probably be applied to any non-fey, including splat book critters. After all, no none-fae can see through the mask without some considerable mojo whether from a fae or their own personal power source. I don't remember reading anything about it, and my players certainly never shown any interest in getting vampires into the world of the Fae (the only other splat book I have been using on occassion as of yet) beyond maybe we can lure that bastard into the Hedge to get rid of the monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T06:19:35-07:00","id":502829,"title":"","content":"Demon and Mummy are easy, as said earlier. Demons start as angels and fall to become Demons, and then that's a point of no return. Mummies start as humans of Item, and then go through the Rite of Return to become Mummies, or spoilers to become the Deceived. Humans can also become Sadikh, which is also, if I remember correctly, a point of no return.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T06:34:34-07:00","id":502839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/498879-vampire-and-werewolf-transformation-diagram-for-crossover-games-large-image?p=502715#post502715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a way enscorcereled mortals could be considered 'fey-touched'. They are basically any mortal that through a deal with a Fae or Changeling can now fully see the world of the Fae. Mind you, that particular template can probably be applied to any non-fey, including splat book critters. After all, no none-fae can see through the mask without some considerable mojo whether from a fae or their own personal power source. I don't remember reading anything about it, and my players certainly never shown any interest in getting vampires into the world of the Fae (the only other splat book I have been using on occassion as of yet) beyond maybe we can lure that bastard into the Hedge to get rid of the monster.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fae touched mortal is another template, it's the result of a true fae kidnapping someone but they leave before they make the full transition into a changeling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/498879-vampire-and-werewolf-transformation-diagram-for-crossover-games-large-image?p=499711#post499711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can, and in fact, they have stats for a hypothetical &quot;Vampiric Promethean&quot; in Saturnine Night (p. 35).</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually that guy is a promethean made by a vampire, not a promethean made from a vampire.<br /> <br /> Anyway, something I thought I'd mention- In the Vampire Chronicler's Guide it offers the option for vampires to regain their mortality, also in the victorian book it has fetches who have become human. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 05-04-2015, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T08:04:17-07:00","id":502926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/498879-vampire-and-werewolf-transformation-diagram-for-crossover-games-large-image?p=502829#post502829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon and Mummy are easy, as said earlier. Demons start as angels and fall to become Demons, and then that's a point of no return.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one of the Demon factions is dedicated to finding a way back.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T08:17:31-07:00","id":502934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/498879-vampire-and-werewolf-transformation-diagram-for-crossover-games-large-image?p=502926#post502926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think one of the Demon factions is dedicated to finding a way back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dedicated but not wholly successful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T09:32:25-07:00","id":503004,"title":"","content":"Also, Demon's can have kids....<br /> <br /> Fractals, Offspring and Latents.<br /> <br /> They are a fun chart all on their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T10:11:08-07:00","id":503044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/498879-vampire-and-werewolf-transformation-diagram-for-crossover-games-large-image?p=502926#post502926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think one of the Demon factions is dedicated to finding a way back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, Integrators. They are not well-liked among the Demon community.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T05:09:33-07:00","id":505261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/498879-vampire-and-werewolf-transformation-diagram-for-crossover-games-large-image?p=499269#post499269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically you can be a <b>Promethean </b>redeemed into a <b>Human </b>who is an [adoptive <b>Wolf-Blooded</b>, who became a <b>Ghoul </b>temporarily [n times], who turned into a <b>Werewolf</b>, who died and was Resurrected into a <b>Wolf-Blooded</b>] [n times] who <u>at some point</u> failed his/her [second] First Change, became a <b>Ghoul </b>once again [n times], died as a Ghoul, became a <b>Revenant</b>, then diablerized some poor vampire and became one of the <b>Kindred</b>. <i>Only then </i>have you reached the point of no return.<br /> <br /> O_O</div> </div> </div> </div>.... Who then is Killed and his Body is used too create a New Promethean to start the Cycle again.....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T06:19:31-07:00","id":505350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/498879-vampire-and-werewolf-transformation-diagram-for-crossover-games-large-image?p=502934#post502934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dedicated but not wholly successful.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, they are fairly successful often, at least for the PCs (rate of NPC success at achieving Hell is up to individual Storytellers). Or turn into an exile. The whole &quot;achieving your goal for Hell&quot; is a major theme of the game that is stated to be achievable as the basis of the game.<br /> <br /> Plus, being turned back into an angel is a result of being caught by a hunter angel, not just being scrapped or recycled. Happens quite frequently. You might end up losing your free will, but there are times a good chunk of your memories remain instead of being completely scrubbed.<br /> <br /> So, bouncing between demon and angel can be frequent, technically. Or divert to Exile and stay there (could actually be a reason why someone was Exiled, in fact).<br /> <br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> More on topic, I'm wondering about the new Mage stuff revealed in that preview ( <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/supporting-cast-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/supporting-ca...the-awakening/</a> ). Mainly, the idea that proximi are supposedly equal to revenants, and implying that sleepwalkers are somehow the equal of ghouls. Considering that sleepwalkers don't seem to be using Awakened Magic, while ghouls use Disciplines, I really have to wonder if that's accurate. <br /> <br /> With the revenants pasted under &quot;Point of No Return,&quot; I'd have put proximus equal to ghouls (half-template), sleepwalkers equal to mortals with the Mortal-only merits in the vampire book as well as blood bound thralls, and then the generic herds as equal to hired sleeper staff. Will have to see the book for final call, but I really think that mortals with Protected, Producer, or Clear Sighted really resonate more with how sleepwalkers are portrayed in the blog than sleepers.<br /> <br /> But, at the moment, I would put Sleeper as an notation under the Any Human block, then Sleepwalker equal to Sons/Daughters and Fed with Vitae, with Proximus on par with Wolf-blood and Ghoul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-06-2015, 09:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T07:03:42-07:00","id":505402,"title":"","content":"I think it does make sense, from a certain point of view. Ghouls are dependent on vampires for their power. No vitae, no disciplines. Revenants, though limited, can function independently. <br /> <br /> Sleepwalkers using awakened magic require imbued items and talismans and the like. They need a connection to a mage. Proximi can use what little power they have without ever meeting one. It's not likely, but it can happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T08:24:04-07:00","id":505562,"title":"","content":"I'm imagining the Angel tasked with making sure someone goes through all those template changes. Or the jaded Demon that would result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T09:15:16-07:00","id":505654,"title":"","content":"It could be a spirit of healing that's the totem of a very large pack somewhere that's doing it. Maybe that pack just has a very... well-traveled ally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T10:46:15-07:00","id":505762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/498879-vampire-and-werewolf-transformation-diagram-for-crossover-games-large-image?p=505402#post505402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it does make sense, from a certain point of view. Ghouls are dependent on vampires for their power. No vitae, no disciplines. Revenants, though limited, can function independently.<br /> <br /> Sleepwalkers using awakened magic require imbued items and talismans and the like. They need a connection to a mage. Proximi can use what little power they have without ever meeting one. It's not likely, but it can happen.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ghouls being dependents is more of a social thing, though - vampire is a game of social predators with drug-addiction overtones. It makes sense within the context of Vampire for ghouls to be dependent for their hit of supernatural power. Meanwhile, Mage is a more mental game.<br /> <br /> I'm not familiar with WtF 2 enough to say that wolf-bloods are depending on Uratha presence to maintain their powers, but its not the impression I've gotten (feedback appreciated on that last bit).<br /> <br /> Meanwhile revenants aren't partial vampires, they're full vampires without a clan and a few issues with holding on to blood. That includes having Humanity instead of Integrity. I don't get the impression that proximi should be considered full mages with Gnosis traits and Wisdom. Though, they apparently DO suffer from paradox, whereas ghouls do not have any weaknesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-06-2015, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T10:58:38-07:00","id":505776,"title":"","content":"Yeah, wolfbloods are sort of in between the two categories, really. Their powers are all innate, and depending on tell some of them actually <i>are</i> werewolves by most out-of-game definitions. I don't know what else one would call somebody who uncontrollably transforms into a huge wolf under the full moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T10:59:14-07:00","id":505777,"title":"","content":"DaveB's most recent Mage post calls out Sleep-Walkers as the Ghoul equivalent and Proximi as akin to Revenants. <br /> He also said Proximi are going to have Integrity not Wisdom and that their paradoxes will take a different shape than Mage's. That said, they'll have access to two Arcana as Merits, so they will have their own Mage-like powers.<br /> <br /> Wolf-Blooded don't have any access to Gifts. There are some Rites that Werewolves can do to turn everyone into wolves or give everyone spirtual Influence. Some Wolf-Blooded (not all) can learn some of the Rites, too. Other than that, there's just the Tells, which is one, relatively minor trick per Wolf-Blooded that typically has a drawback. There are a couple that allow shape-shifting, but it's just to one form and they either have to tend to an imobile pet or deal wait until someone brandishes religious paraphernalia at them or go into the death rage to make use of it. Where that puts them in terms of mechanical analogs seems a little ambiguous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T11:00:52-07:00","id":505780,"title":"","content":"I guess that just goes to show that, outside of &quot;pure mortal&quot; and &quot;full supernatural template&quot; there's a lot of grey area that's not easily defined and put in a chart, I guess.<br /> <br /> Maybe we should be moving away from &quot;half-templates&quot; as some kind of equivalents between games? I mean, look at Prommies. While there are mortal alchemists as antagonists, they're mortal antagonists, and there's no part-human friend equivalent. The Prommies on this chart are actually backwards - there's only one way they go, and that's actually from nothing to human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-06-2015, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T12:40:06-07:00","id":505974,"title":"","content":"@BarbeChenue: The discussion has gotten fairly far off from your &quot;hey look at this Werewolf/Vampire crossover chart I made&quot;. What did you use to make your original chart? Maybe the rest of us can run with it to make more/bigger ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T17:17:57-07:00","id":506248,"title":"","content":"I used Excel 2007, a lot of customized &quot;predefined shapes&quot; and arrows. The idea came up when I was toying with ideas on how to allow the players more explicit choices in what they could play (saying it's &quot;allowed&quot; doesn't mean people will go out of their way to try it if it's kind of hidden in an appendix chapter). Since the only cross-over I will allow in my own game is Werewolf + Vampire, when I make additions to the initial diagram, it will be for completeness's sake and educational purpose. I strongly doubt most players really need to be &quot;spoiled&quot; of all the supernaturals, but it would be useful for GMs.<br /> <br /> At the moment, since there seems to be many things in motion, and I'm not super familiar with the other lines, I'll wait for 100% sure / concise explanations. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Meanwhile, here's the base Excel file for those who want to tinker with it !<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.filedropper.com/nwod-crossover-diagram\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.filedropper.com/nwod-crossover-diagram\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.filedropper.com/nwod-crossover-diagram\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.filedropper.com/nwod-crossover-diagram </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5602,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","user":"BarbeChenue","date":". 05-06-2015, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T15:16:09-07:00","id":507263,"title":"","content":"I fully updated the diagram to include Prometheans (easy), Mages (and their &quot;support cast&quot;), Changelings and Fae-Touched, as well as Sin-Eaters/Bound.<br /> <br /> <s>I did add a &quot;wolf-blooded X&quot; thing to those who could retain their Tell.</s> I don't know if Proxius turned into Vampires retain Arcana or Mage Merits, or if Changelings can keep their former &quot;ghoul&quot; Merits. It's all pretty complicated. Also, I didn't know much about the Fae-Touched / Sleepwalkers, so I assumed everyone could be Fae-Touched or Sleepwalkers, and that it would be equivalent to other Merit-Based minor templates. Proxius are not clear at all either, so I don't know if you can be a wolf-blooded fey-fouched sleepwalker ghoul Proxius (all Proxius <i>are </i>sleepwalkers anyway).<br /> <br /> Sorry if it's a bit of a mess, blame the minor templates and their endless (literally) cross-overs.<br /> v1: <a href=\"http://i58.tinypic.com/2gv37n6.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://i58.tinypic.com/2gv37n6.jpg</a><br /> v2: <a href=\"http://i61.tinypic.com/2r7txqb.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://i61.tinypic.com/2r7txqb.jpg</a><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i61.tinypic.com/2r7txqb.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5602,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","user":"BarbeChenue","date":". 05-07-2015, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T16:47:24-07:00","id":507359,"title":"","content":"I made a spoiler-free version for my players:<br /> <br /> Linky: <a href=\"http://i57.tinypic.com/qot2z5.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://i57.tinypic.com/qot2z5.jpg</a><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i57.tinypic.com/qot2z5.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T18:05:36-07:00","id":507453,"title":"","content":"General note that Unbinding doesn't make you a human - it makes you one of the Vacant, i.e. a Sin-Eater without a geist.<br /> <br /> Also, the word is spelled &quot;fae-touched,&quot; and the changeover point for becoming a changeling is more specifically partaking of the nature of Arcadia through the Fae's patronage - &quot;Abducted to Faerie&quot; would probably be a better phrasing, since rescuing a loved one before they become a changeling is a fairly common &quot;back to Arcadia&quot; storyhook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T19:17:06-07:00","id":507490,"title":"","content":"Yes I think the Vacant can still use rituals or something?<br /> <br /> Also, Wolf-Blooded and ghouls can still become every other major template that one can become.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T20:16:18-07:00","id":507560,"title":"","content":"The Vacant can use one Ceremony, which is a re-Binding and is specifically called out with &quot;this profane ceremony shouldn't even <i>work</i>&quot;. They get to keep a Psyche of 1, which gives them a slight boost to resisting supernatural stuff and lets them spend plasm if they can come by it. I guess that makes them not quite human.<br /> There is a paragraph or two in the Geist book about resolving your geist. Its a process akin to helping a ghost pass on, after which you're a Sin-Eater without a geist. It's intentionally left vague as to what that makes you, whether Mortal or otherwise.<br /> <br /> I really appreciate that you've gone trough the trouble of making this image. That's great. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T21:31:49-07:00","id":507630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/498879-vampire-and-werewolf-transformation-diagram-for-crossover-games-large-image?p=507490#post507490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Wolf-Blooded and ghouls can still become every other major template that one can become.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the (intentionally) pale lines tangling between the mid/lower rows are meant to represent that. I should add more perhaps between the mid boxes (ghoul, etc.) and the top ones (Embrace, Awakening, etc.).<br /> <br /> Edit: New image, hopefully I'm getting it right ! (Your feedback <i>is </i>appreciated, btw !)<br /> <br /> Linky: <a href=\"http://i58.tinypic.com/2m49f8j.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://i58.tinypic.com/2m49f8j.jpg</a><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i58.tinypic.com/2m49f8j.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Notes/Assumptions:<ul><li>that in the rare case of &quot;spontaneous First Change&quot; by apparently non-wolf-blooded, it is preceded by a quick &quot;Adoption&quot; as wolf-blooded.</li> <li>that one <i>becomes fae-touched</i> (even if the Merit wasn't purchased) when Abducted, since the condition seems to be more than met, I didn't add lines to the &quot;Abducted to Faerie&quot; box.</li> <li>I <i>did </i>add lines, however, towards &quot;Awakening&quot;, since there really didn't seem to be any obligation to be a Sleepwalker or Proxius/Proximi first. I hesitated, since Sleepwalker is such a vast and wide category, any Template seems to qualify.</li> <li>I also assumed that almost anyone could be a &quot;Potential Bound&quot;.</li> </ul><br /> I'll work on the Arisen (Mummy: The Curse) and the Unchained (Demon: The Descent) later on.<br /> <br /> Is there a listing of all the existing Templates, minor or major ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5602,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","user":"BarbeChenue","date":". 05-08-2015, 01:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T23:57:04-07:00","id":507758,"title":"","content":"I would not include 'Hedge' in the abducted section. Everybody can end up in the Hedge, even by accident, and while the Hedge is murder on ones Integrity, and given time is prone to turn Vampires and Werewolves in the murdering machines that have lost all semblance of humanity and takes away the Mages ability to cast spells, you only become a Changeling once you reach Arcadia and somehow manage to get back. People who enter the Hedge and get back in time suffer no adverse effects beyond the damage to their Integrity and their splat variants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T08:42:56-07:00","id":508125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/498879-vampire-and-werewolf-transformation-diagram-for-crossover-games-large-image?p=507630#post507630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>I <i>did </i>add lines, however, towards &quot;Awakening&quot;, since there really didn't seem to be any obligation to be a Sleepwalker or Proxius/Proximi first. I hesitated, since Sleepwalker is such a vast and wide category, any Template seems to qualify.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Mage developer said all templates are sleepwalkers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T12:55:02-07:00","id":508338,"title":"","content":"All templates, plus anyone with any sort of supernatural merit. <br /> <br /> Although I'm now wondering if ex-ghouls keep the trait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T14:03:52-08:00","id":794375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/498879-vampire-and-werewolf-transformation-diagram-for-crossover-games-large-image?p=507630#post507630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a listing of all the existing Templates, minor or major ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never seen a listing anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5544-ancientswordrage","name":"AncientSwordRage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T14:40:33-08:00","id":794393,"title":"","content":"Awesome, I tried working on this once and gave up when it started to get all too complicated. Love that you've kept going and made it so comprehensive, well done. This is looking so accurate now and I love that I can show this to my players if they ever get confused.<br /> <br /> I also love seeing every arrow going more or less in the same direction, then having Prometheans go against the flow trying to reach human. I just think that one visual really captures so much about the game and how its themes work.<br /> <br /> By the way, you were mentioning creating this in Excel. I just thought I'd mention VUE in case you're not aware of it. It makes doing charts like this really easy and is completely open source freeware. It's what I use for all my roleplaying flow-charts. <a href=\"http://vue.tufts.edu/\" target=\"_blank\">http://vue.tufts.edu/</a> if you want to take a look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T13:43:12-08:00","id":827755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/498879-vampire-and-werewolf-transformation-diagram-for-crossover-games-large-image?p=794393#post794393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awesome, I tried working on this once and gave up when it started to get all too complicated. Love that you've kept going and made it so comprehensive, well done. This is looking so accurate now and I love that I can show this to my players if they ever get confused.<br /> <br /> I also love seeing every arrow going more or less in the same direction, then having Prometheans go against the flow trying to reach human. I just think that one visual really captures so much about the game and how its themes work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the encouragement! I'm looking forward to updating the diagram once the dust settles on the newer products (like the newest Mage, and perhaps templates from Hurt Locker, if any), and I'd love to expand on it with other lines (not sure about which ones yet though).<br /> <br /> As for Excel, I mostly use it out of personal quirk. I make all my character sheets on it, and I don't know why, but it's the most &quot;hypnotic&quot; software out there with Photoshop. Time flies when I'm on a project...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T04:33:34-07:00","id":1217929,"title":"","content":"What effect would the Resurrection Numen have on Vampires, Sin-Eaters and Prometheans? or Beasts and Remade for that matter? I'm assuming that the Rite of Return for Mummies is too strong to be altered or undone by that Numen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T05:53:24-07:00","id":1217938,"title":"","content":"It's in the description of the Numen:<br /> &quot;Supernatural beings that have already died as part of their transformation \u2014 vampires, mummies, and Sin-Eaters \u2014 can\u2019t be resurrected, nor can anyone who died of natural causes. Other supernatural beings lose their powers when resurrected. Mages become Sleepwalkers, and werewolves, wolf-blooded.&quot;<br /> <br /> Prometheans would probably not be resurrected since they too would lose their supernatural qualities, and their raw materials weren't alive when they were created.<br /> Beasts would simply become human.<br /> The Remade would either become human or remain dead, depending on if they died as part of the transformation to a Deviant. Unless there's a Sleepwalker style subsplat for Deviant, but I highly doubt that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}